<title>UK: ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</title>
<headline>ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) said the 4,250 tonne buffer-stock sale earlier on Tuesday was completed at the following prices -</p>
<p> ORIGIN	TONNES	QUALITY	     US$/TONNE</p>
<p> Ivory Coast   100	    GF		 $1,382</p>
<p> Ivory Coast   673	    GF		 $1,405-$1,413</p>
<p> Ivory Coast   251	    FF		 $1,382</p>
<p> Ivory Coast    61	    FF		 $1,337</p>
<p> Ghana	   278	    GF		 $1,374</p>
<p> Ghana	   907	    GF		 $1,405-$1,428</p>
<p> Ghana	   292	    FF		 $1,353</p>
<p> Nigeria	 351	    GF		 $1,335</p>
<p> Nigeria	 160	    GF		 $1,369</p>
<p> Nigeria	 375	    FF		 $1,306</p>
<p> Cameroon	105	   FAQ		 $1,289</p>
<p> Ivory Coast   335	   FAQ		 $1,250-$1,283</p>
<p> Ivory Coast    33	   FAQ		 $1,260</p>
<p> Nigeria	  82	   FAQ		 $1,250</p>
<p> Nigeria	 100	   FAQ		 $1,257</p>
<p> Nigeria	 148	   FAQ		 $1,365</p>
<p>(GF=good fermented, FF=fair fermented, FAQ=fair average quality)</p>
<p>The ICCO said the prices were for prompt delivery.</p>
<p>--Jalil Hamid, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
